IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-index.l4: Part 35 "The registrar's index of company names", ss 1099 to 1101 of the Companies Act 2006
-- (lines 15776-15806 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. The Act's index (Schedule 8) says "registrar's index of company names" is
-- defined by s 1099: `s 1099(1) the index is the registrar's index of company names`.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. ss 1099(4)-(5) (the Secretary of State's order-making power) and s 1101 (the Secretary of State's
-- power to amend enactments by regulations) are machinery: inert (reason 2) in NOTES.md.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`).

§ `Part 35: the registrar's index of company names (ss 1099 to 1101)`

-- ---- s 1099 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The bodies named in s 1099(2) and (3). The text has two paragraphs lettered (f) in subsection (3); they are told apart
-- below by "first" and "second" in the order the text gives them (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 1099 kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1099(2)(a) a UK-registered company`
    `s 1099(2)(b) a body to which a provision of the Companies Acts applies by virtue of regulations under section 1043 (unregistered companies)`
    `s 1099(2)(c) an overseas company that has registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046`
    `s 1099(3)(a) a limited partnership registered in the United Kingdom (within the meaning of section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907)`
    `s 1099(3)(b) a limited liability partnership incorporated in the United Kingdom`
    `s 1099(3)(c) a UK Economic Interest Grouping`
    `s 1099(3)(ca) an EEIG establishment, within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the European Economic Interest Grouping Regulations 1989`
    `s 1099(3)(d) an open-ended investment company authorised in the United Kingdom`
    `s 1099(3)(e) a society registered under the Industrial and Provident Societies Act 1965 or the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014`
    `s 1099(3)(f) first paragraph (f): a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017`
    `s 1099(3)(f) second paragraph (f): a charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Part 11 of the Charities Act 2011`
    `s 1099(3)(g) a Scottish charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Chapter 7, Part 1 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`
    `s 1099 any other body`

-- src:15780 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:15781 | (a) UK-registered companies;
-- src:15782 | (b) any body to which any provision of the Companies Acts applies by virtue of regulations under section 1043 (unregistered companies); and
-- src:15783 | (c) overseas companies that have registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046, other than companies that appear to the registrar not to be required to do so.
-- src:15784 | (3) This section also applies to—
-- src:15785 | (a) limited partnerships registered in the United Kingdom (within the meaning of section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907);
-- src:15786 | (b) limited liability partnerships incorporated in the United Kingdom;
-- src:15787 | (c) UK Economic Interest Groupings;
-- src:15788 | (ca) EEIG establishments, within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the European Economic Interest Grouping Regulations 1989;
-- src:15789 | (d) open-ended investment companies authorised in the United Kingdom;
-- src:15790 | (e) societies registered under the Industrial and Provident Societies Act 1965 (c. 12) or the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014.
-- src:15791 | (f) protected cell companies registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017.
-- src:15792 | (f) charitable incorporated organisations within the meaning of Part 11 of the Charities Act 2011;
-- src:15793 | (g) Scottish charitable incorporated organisations within the meaning of Chapter 7, Part 1 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 (asp 10)
@ref s 1099(2)-(3) The bodies to which the section applies (src:15780-15793)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1099 kind of body`
      `the overseas company appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1099(2)(a) a UK-registered company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(2)(b) a body to which a provision of the Companies Acts applies by virtue of regulations under section 1043 (unregistered companies)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(2)(c) an overseas company that has registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046` THEN
        IF `the overseas company appears to the registrar not to be required to register particulars`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "overseas companies that have registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046, other than companies that appear to the registrar not to be required to do so"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(a) a limited partnership registered in the United Kingdom (within the meaning of section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(b) a limited liability partnership incorporated in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(c) a UK Economic Interest Grouping` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(ca) an EEIG establishment, within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the European Economic Interest Grouping Regulations 1989` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(d) an open-ended investment company authorised in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(e) a society registered under the Industrial and Provident Societies Act 1965 or the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(f) first paragraph (f): a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(f) second paragraph (f): a charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Part 11 of the Charities Act 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099(3)(g) a Scottish charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Chapter 7, Part 1 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1099 any other body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the lists of subsections (2) and (3) are not closed by "only", and subsection (4) lets the Secretary of State add bodies by order

-- src:15778 | (1) The registrar of companies must keep an index of the names of the companies and other bodies to which this section applies.
-- src:15779 | This is “the registrar's index of company names”.
@ref s 1099(1) The registrar must keep an index of the names of the bodies to which the section applies (src:15778-15779)
GIVEN `the section applies to the body` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1099(1) the registrar must keep the body's name in the index` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies to the body`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an index of the names of the companies and other bodies to which this section applies" says what the duty covers and not that the registrar may not keep other names
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): whether the section applies to the body is not decided by subsections (2) and (3)

@ref s 1099(1) "the registrar's index of company names" (src:15779)
GIVEN `the index is the index, kept by the registrar, of the names of the companies and other bodies to which section 1099 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1099(1) the index is the registrar's index of company names` MEANS
    IF `the index is the index, kept by the registrar, of the names of the companies and other bodies to which section 1099 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is “the registrar's index of company names”"

-- ---- s 1100 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15799 | Any person may inspect the registrar's index of company names.
@ref s 1100 Any person may inspect the index (src:15799)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
